      "tilling_destroys_mycorrhizal_networks_": "Tilling destroys mycorrhizal networks (this is why no-till farming is gaining traction). Chemical fertilizers can suppress fungal growth — the plant gets \"lazy\" and stops feeding its fungal partner. Garlic mustard (an invasive) releases chemicals that specifically destroy mycorrhizal fungi, devastating the entire underground ecosystem.",
