      "uscg_33_cfr_part_175_equipment_require": "USCG 33 CFR Part 175 — Equipment requirements",
      "use_a_boat_kayak_canoe_paddleboard_row": "Use a boat — kayak, canoe, paddleboard, rowboat. Approach with the bow toward the victim. Have them grab the back, not the side. NEVER let them climb in over the side — they will flip you. Tow them to shore.",
      "use_neon_yellow_orange_or_pink_never_b": "Use NEON YELLOW, ORANGE, or PINK. NEVER blue, green, white, or gray — those colors are nearly invisible against pool bottoms or lake water. This single change can mean the difference between a lifeguard spotting a submerged child in 5 seconds vs 50.",
      "used_by_water_polo_players_lifeguards_": "Used by water polo players, lifeguards, and anyone needing to stay vertical in deep water for a long time. Each leg traces a circle in the opposite direction, generating continuous upward thrust without the up-and-down bobbing of a flutter kick.",
      "vermont_fish_wildlife_ice_safety_guide": "Vermont Fish & Wildlife — Ice Safety Guidelines",
      "virginia_graeme_baker_pool_spa_safety_": "Virginia Graeme Baker Pool & Spa Safety Act",
      "wasted_energy_suboptimal_length_or_kic": "Wasted energy. Suboptimal length or kick.",
      "water_hazards": " water hazards, ",
      "wave_one_arm_and_yell_a_lifeguard_or_b": " Wave one arm and yell. A lifeguard or bystander can throw a flotation device. The current will eventually weaken (rip currents end past the breakers).",
      "wearable_id_with_name_diagnosis_family": "Wearable ID with name, diagnosis, family contact. Important if the child elopes and is found by strangers who may misinterpret behavior as defiance, intoxication, or hostility.",
      "what_happens_with_super_fast_rate_but_": "What happens with super-fast rate but tiny length?",
      "when_you_fall_in_cold_water_the_worst_": "When you fall in cold water, the worst thing is to try to swim immediately. Tilt your head back, fill your lungs, and float. Your gasp reflex will pass in 60 seconds or so. Then you can swim or signal. This single instruction has saved thousands of lives. ",
      "whoever_saves_a_single_soul_scripture_": "\"Whoever saves a single soul, scripture considers it as if they saved an entire world.\"",
      "whoever_saves_a_single_soul_scripture__2": "\"Whoever saves a single soul, scripture considers it as if they saved an entire world.\"",
      "why_life_jackets_work": "Why Life Jackets Work",
      "wilderness_medical_society": "Wilderness Medical Society",
      "wilderness_medical_society_practice_gu": "Wilderness Medical Society — Practice Guidelines for Hypothermia",
      "without_becoming_the_second_victim": " without becoming the second victim.",
      "ymca_aquatic_standards": "YMCA Aquatic Standards",
      "ymca_aquatics_programs": "YMCA — Aquatics Programs",
      "ymca_aquatics_programs_2": "YMCA — Aquatics programs",
      "you_buy_a_child_s_life_jacket_you_do_t": "You buy a child's life jacket. You do the lift test on shore: when you lift at the shoulders, the jacket comes up to the child's ears. The salesperson says it will be fine in the water and the child will \"grow into it.\" What do you do?",
      "you_cannot_help_someone_you_do_not_rea": "You cannot help someone you do not realize is drowning. And once you realize it, the strongest urge is to jump in. Both of those instincts are wrong. This module covers ",
      "you_cannot_learn_to_swim_from_a_screen": "You cannot learn to swim from a screen. Find a Water Safety Instructor at Red Cross or YMCA.",
      "you_have_time_the_1_1_10_rule_applies_": "You have time. The 1-1-10 rule applies (1 minute to control breathing, 10 minutes of useful arm strength, 1 hour before unconsciousness). Use that first minute deliberately.",
      "you_missed": "You missed ",
      "you_see_a_person_fall_through_ice_on_a": "You see a person fall through ice on a pond about 100 feet from shore. There is a long rope in your truck. You can ice skate. Two strangers are nearby. What is your best move?",
      "you_will_exhaust_yourself_and_drown_th": " You will exhaust yourself and drown. The current is faster than you can swim.",
